I also had a very lucky game, this was game where I found four
randomly-generated artifacts laying around the dungeon by the castle.

> +0 Gauntlets of Power, lying around in the dungeon
> +4 Shield of Reflection, dropped by a hill orc in Sokoban (yes, +4!)
> +0 Gray Dragon Scales, left by a gray dragon which must've been the result
> of a polytrap in the Mines.

Get the gray dragon scales upgraded as soon as you can.  Gray dragon
scale mail is probably *the* most important non-required thing in an
ascension.  You could go with black or silver, true, but in practice
you can often survive without reflection or disintegration-resistance,
while lack of magic resistance will probably kill you sooner, later,
or much later.  And the AC of dragon scale mail is almost sinful.

> Currently Expert in dagger, and wielding Sting (#named).  Also have myself a
> nice pet rock troll.

The troll is nice to have.  When playing my Tourist, I actually didn't
use most of those artifacts for half the game -- most of them weren't
that useful in a general situation.  As a Tourist, you're the only
class who can get at least to Basic in every weapon in the game, and
Sting isn't really that useful.  A two-handed sword is the weapon I
went with, and it got me surprisingly far.  I'd swap between it and
Magicbane.  I eventually found Mjollnir in the Castle, but I could
have won with the sword once it got to +6.  But you can also go with a
dwarvish mattock, the canonical most damaging artifact weapon.

If you don't have poison resistance, get it.  Since you have Gauntlets
of Power, you can eat poisonous corpses without worrying about
strength loss, so it should be simple to get.  Of course there are the
other usuals, too: fire/cold/shock/sleep resistance for example.

